  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 111 PM MST Fri Nov 27 2026\n\nToday Through The Weekend...\n High pressure continues to dominate the \narea this afternoon into the evening. Skies will remain mostly sunny \nwith a few high clouds moving in late this evening with temps \nclimbing to the upper 60s. This weekend will be dry with fair \nweather, above normal temps will be around on saturday with highs in \nthe low to mid 70s. A shortwave trough will move into the area \nSaturday afternoon. This will create a jetstreak that will increase \nwinds at the surface. Winds will gust up to 35 mph in the lowlands \nwith gusts up to 45 mph in elevated areas. A backdoor cold front \nassociated with the shortwave will bring temperatures back down to \nnear normal on Sunday with highs climbing to the upper 50s to low \n60s throughout the CWA.\n\nMonday and Tuesday...\n Zonal flow will return to the area Monday and \nparts of Tuesday this will return above normal temps to the region \nwith highs climbing into the low 70s, with Fair weather. A few \nshortwave ripples will move through the area late Tuesday that will \nbring breezy winds to the Sacramento and Gila mountains with \ngusts up to 40 mph in those areas. \n\nWednesday and Beyond...\n Our next chance for Precipitation will come \nlater next week with a deep upper level trough that will shift \nthrough the area. Models differ on the arrival of the trough but it \nwill be within the Wednesday/Thursday timeframe. Scattered rain \nshowers will move through the area during this timeframe with the\npotential for some accumulating snow in higher elevated areas.",
